esqlQuery.esql:
TS metrics-supabase.metrics.otel-*
// node_vmstat_oom_kill is a monotonic kernel counter published as a gauge, so DELTA()
// gives the number of new kills inside the window.
| STATS
    `OOM Kills` = SUM(DELTA(node_vmstat_oom_kill)),
    `Peak Kill Count` = MAX(MAX_OVER_TIME(node_vmstat_oom_kill)),
    `Available Memory Bytes` = MIN(MIN_OVER_TIME(node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes))
  BY resource.attributes.supabase_project_ref
// A node reboot zeroes the counter, making DELTA negative; fall back to the peak so a kill
// that preceded the reboot is not missed.
| EVAL `Counter Reset` = `OOM Kills` < 0
// A single OOM kill means the kernel terminated a process; never expected in normal operation.
| WHERE `OOM Kills` > 0 OR (`Counter Reset` AND `Peak Kill Count` > 0)
